        # does not need one thread-block per chunk of work. Launching an
        # extremely large grid (one wave per chunk) causes an under-filled
        # tail wave at the end of the kernel, which lowers achieved
        # occupancy relative to the theoretical maximum. Cap the grid to a
        # size proportional to the number of SMs so that blocks are
        # resident for the whole kernel lifetime and the stride loop
        # inside the kernel covers the remaining elements, improving
        # achieved occupancy without changing kernel semantics.
